          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Classically in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+geometry"} complex geometry
            %em elliptic curve
            is a connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            (a connected compact 1-dimensional
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
            1, hence it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            equipped with the structure of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structure"} conformal structure
          %p
            The curious term “elliptic” is a remnant from the 19th century, a back-formation which refers to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+functions"} elliptic functions
            (generalizing circular functions, i.e., the classical trigonometric functions) and their natural domains as Riemann surfaces.
          %p
            In more modern frameworks and in the generality of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            or indeed over any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            may be defined as a complete irreducible non-singular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
            of
            = succeed "-1" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+genus"} arithmetic genus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
          %p Elliptic curves have many remarkable properties, and their deeper arithmetic study is one of the most profound subjects in present-day mathematics.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            equipped with its canonical map to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+formal+group+laws"} moduli stack of formal group laws
            plays a central role in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+level"} chromatic level
            2, where it serves to parameterize
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology+theories"} elliptic cohomology theories
          %p
            Elliptic curves over the complex numbers are also interpreted as those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            are the
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
            this connects to to the role of elliptic curves in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology+theory"} elliptic cohomology theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionOverGeneralRing Over a general ring
          %p
            Elliptic curves over a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            (hence in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            parameterized over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} prime spectrum
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OverGeneralRingConceptualDefinition"} Conceptual definition
          %p
            More concretely there are various explicit and standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinazations
            of elliptic curves as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations"} equations
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OverGeneralRingAsSolutionsToEquations"} Coordinatized as solutions to cubic equations
          %h4#OverGeneralRingConceptualDefinition Conceptual definition
          %p
          #DefinitionEllipticCurve.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              An
              %strong elliptic curve
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
              (a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
              that is a relative 1-dimensional,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+scheme"} proper
              curve over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
