              = succeed "." do
                %em ordinary
          %h4#OverGeneralRingAsSolutionsToEquations Coordinatized as solutions to cubic Weierstrass equations
          %p
            Elliptic curves are examples of solutions to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diophantine+equations"} Diophantine equations
            of degree 3. We start by giving the equation valued over general rings, which is fairly complicated compared to the special case that it reduces to in the classical case over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
          %p
            (See
            %a{:href => "#Silverman09"} Silverman 09, III.1
            for a textbook account and for instance (
            %a{:href => "#QuickIntro"}> QuickIntro
            ) for a quick survey.)
          %h5#WeierstrassCubicDiscriminantAndJInvariant
            Weierstrass cubic, discriminant and
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
